WEBVTT


00:00:29.248 --> 00:00:30.688
The question of happiness


00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:32.813
has preoccupied
philosophers, poets


00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.532
and pharmaceutical companies
for thousands of years.


00:00:36.688 --> 00:00:39.208
Clearly, it's a tricky one.


00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:42.128
When I graduated from
design school three years ago,


00:00:42.287 --> 00:00:45.015
I had a definite plan.


00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:48.768
Couple months at home,
put together a kickass portfolio,


00:00:48.927 --> 00:00:51.971
then I'd take Manhattan
by storm.


00:00:54.326 --> 00:00:55.887
And here is home.


00:00:56.887 --> 00:00:58.327
West Orange, New Jersey.


00:00:58.486 --> 00:01:00.091
Nice, huh?


00:01:01.687 --> 00:01:04.807
OK, it's not Manhattan,
but, like I say, it's temporary.


00:01:04.966 --> 00:01:08.730
I grew up here
with two families.


00:01:08.886 --> 00:01:11.570
That's my dad in blue,
and that's his best friend, Terry.


00:01:11.726 --> 00:01:13.570
The Inseparables.


00:01:13.726 --> 00:01:16.814
They go jogging together
three times a week without fail.


00:01:16.965 --> 00:01:19.126
You can set your clock by it.


00:01:19.285 --> 00:01:22.046
You could say life in the Oranges
is dependable.


00:01:22.205 --> 00:01:24.169
I can't believe
you made me do this.


00:01:24.325 --> 00:01:27.053
Good for your appetite.
See you in an hour.


00:01:27.205 --> 00:01:30.293
You can depend on Terry
to have a gadget for everything.


00:01:30.445 --> 00:01:33.172
Walked 1.2 miles.
Only stopped twice.


00:01:33.324 --> 00:01:34.645
That's great, honey.


00:01:34.804 --> 00:01:36.691
And you can
depend on Cathy


00:01:36.844 --> 00:01:38.644
to never hear
a single word he says.


00:01:38.804 --> 00:01:40.484
Make sure you put your bicycle
in the garage.


00:01:40.644 --> 00:01:42.488
And pull the pork
out of the freezer, honey.


00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:47.851
Across the street,
our house.


00:01:48.004 --> 00:01:50.371
Every year,
my mom gets more involved


00:01:50.524 --> 00:01:51.887
with her carolling group.


00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:53.844
They start rehearsing
in August.


00:01:54.003 --> 00:01:55.563
# Jingle bells
Jingle all the way... #


00:01:55.723 --> 00:01:58.288
And every year, my dad
hates them a little bit more.


00:02:01.323 --> 00:02:05.164
OK, sure. I'm still here.
I'm a few years behind in my plan.


00:02:05.323 --> 00:02:07.090
But you can't
rush these things.


00:02:07.243 --> 00:02:10.091
Portfolios need
to be perfect, right?


00:02:10.242 --> 00:02:12.882
Plus I have a day job
working in furniture, so...


00:02:13.042 --> 00:02:16.402
...as far as I was concerned,
everything was on track.


00:02:16.562 --> 00:02:19.606
# Happy birthday to you... #


00:02:19.761 --> 00:02:22.609
That is, until what
happened... happened


00:02:22.762 --> 00:02:24.846
Nina Ostroff.


00:02:25.001 --> 00:02:27.685
When all this started,
she was at a safe distance,


00:02:27.841 --> 00:02:29.881
3, 000 miles away
in San Francisco.


00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:33.685
I Happy birthday to you. I


00:02:33.841 --> 00:02:36.165
Make a wish, babe.


00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.808
And I was the fifth wheel


00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.208
to our parents'
regular Saturday foursome.


00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.040
Say it again.


00:02:50.199 --> 00:02:51.487
OK.


00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.963
Un coup de birch.


00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.603
Hey, Vanny.


00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.243
I read the most
interesting article


00:02:57.399 --> 00:02:59.167
called 'The IKEA Conspiracy',


00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:00.924
which you'd be
really fascinated by.


00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:02.400
- What it imagines is a...
- Terry?


00:03:02.559 --> 00:03:04.042
We need to call Nina.
We said 9:30.


00:03:04.199 --> 00:03:05.639
I'm on it.


00:03:05.799 --> 00:03:08.003
Vanessa, did you look at
that one-bedroom in Fort Lee?


00:03:08.158 --> 00:03:11.323
Yeah. It was, um, like a closet
in the basement.


00:03:11.478 --> 00:03:12.842
There's always something, honey.


00:03:12.998 --> 00:03:14.319
Don't be so choosy.
Nothing's perfect.


00:03:14.478 --> 00:03:16.639
There was, you know,
one window.


00:03:16.798 --> 00:03:18.642
- Paige, did I tell you...
- No room to breathe.


00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.478
...that Joan Marshack
was the listing agent on that?


00:03:20.638 --> 00:03:23.442
David, you are going
to really love this.


00:03:23.598 --> 00:03:28.399
This speaker box communicates
wirelessly with my cell phone.


00:03:28.558 --> 00:03:30.642
And guess where
I read about it first.


00:03:30.797 --> 00:03:32.805
'Consumer Reports'. Thank you
so much for the subscription.


00:03:32.958 --> 00:03:35.206
- I'm really enjoying it.
- You are consumingly welcome.


00:03:35.357 --> 00:03:38.445
I don't even have to take
my cell phone out of my pocket.


00:03:38.597 --> 00:03:39.918
Watch.


00:03:40.077 --> 00:03:41.921
Dial Nina.


00:03:42.077 --> 00:03:43.517
Please repeat request.


00:03:43.676 --> 00:03:44.997
Dial Nina.


00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:47.241
Maybe your pants
are blocking the signal.


00:03:47.396 --> 00:03:48.836
They're cotton.


00:03:50.276 --> 00:03:52.916
Nina's cell phone, dialling.


00:03:54.716 --> 00:03:57.717
Nina - their daughter
and my best friend


00:03:57.876 --> 00:03:59.884
from ages 0
to high school.


00:04:00.036 --> 00:04:02.436
We spent hours together
planning our big escape.


00:04:02.596 --> 00:04:04.560
I'm gonna live in New York.


00:04:04.715 --> 00:04:06.036
And Paris.


00:04:06.195 --> 00:04:08.443
And I'm gonna be a famous chef
and have a million lovers


00:04:08.595 --> 00:04:09.916
who'll take me
all over the world


00:04:10.075 --> 00:04:12.203
so I never have to come back
to New Jersey again.


00:04:12.355 --> 00:04:15.082
It's like
there's no air here, right?


00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:16.839
Totally.


00:04:19.514 --> 00:04:20.955
You'll come too, right?


00:04:21.114 --> 00:04:23.034
Are you kidding?


00:04:24.235 --> 00:04:26.002
Until sophomore year,


00:04:26.154 --> 00:04:30.442
when she abandoned me for
Liz Gaines and the Fun Bunch.


00:04:33.034 --> 00:04:37.234
She also kissed and later gave
a hand job to Peter Fortunate.


00:04:37.394 --> 00:04:40.514
I'd been secretly
in love with him forever.


00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:43.597
Then, just as her parents
were lining her up


00:04:43.753 --> 00:04:45.553
at some lame college
in Pennsylvania,


00:04:45.713 --> 00:04:48.157
she decided she was
going to travel the world.


00:04:48.313 --> 00:04:50.757
Or at least those parts


00:04:50.912 --> 00:04:52.832
that were out of
her mothefs cell phone range.


00:04:56.232 --> 00:04:57.879
Hello?


00:04:58.032 --> 00:05:00.432
Happy birthday, sweetie!


00:05:00.592 --> 00:05:02.240
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday, Nina.


00:05:02.392 --> 00:05:05.240
It's David and Paige.
Vanessa's here too.


00:05:05.392 --> 00:05:07.116
It's true. I'm here.


00:05:07.272 --> 00:05:08.560
Hey, Ethan.


00:05:08.711 --> 00:05:11.439
I think Nina's fucking parents
are on the phone.


00:05:13.192 --> 00:05:15.636
I didn't know I was having
a party. It was a surprise.


00:05:15.791 --> 00:05:17.875
Honey, we can't hear you.


00:05:18.031 --> 00:05:20.638
Ethan threw me
a surprise party.


00:05:20.791 --> 00:05:22.515
It's so great.


00:05:22.671 --> 00:05:23.992
Did you guys get
the pictures I sent?


00:05:24.151 --> 00:05:25.875
Yes, we did.


00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:27.711
More young men should have earrings
in their face.


00:05:27.871 --> 00:05:30.271
What? I'm sorry, I can't
hear you. Am I on speaker?


00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.151
Nina, what day are you
flying in for Thanksgiving?


00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.354
Thanksgiving. Mom, um...


00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.354
Uh, I don't think I'm gonna
make it for Thanksgiving.


00:05:41.509 --> 00:05:44.630
Ethan's photography show's
next weekend, and it's a big deal.


00:05:44.789 --> 00:05:46.589
Sweetie, we haven't
seen you for two years.


00:05:46.749 --> 00:05:48.113
You haven't been home
in five years.


00:05:48.269 --> 00:05:49.994
Since we visited you.
That's a long time.


00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:51.469
Um...


00:05:51.629 --> 00:05:53.637
Can you take me
off speaker, please?


00:05:53.789 --> 00:05:55.230
Sorry, sweetie,
I'd have to disconnect you


00:05:55.389 --> 00:05:57.353
to take you off speaker -
it's a very complex system.


00:05:57.509 --> 00:05:58.513
OK.


00:05:59.908 --> 00:06:02.757
Look, you're not
gonna like this, but...


00:06:02.908 --> 00:06:04.992
Ethan and I
are getting married.


00:06:05.148 --> 00:06:08.269
He proposed two weeks ago
on his birthday.


00:06:08.428 --> 00:06:10.032
He took me out
to Baker Beach,


00:06:10.188 --> 00:06:11.508
which overlooks
the Golden Gate Bridge,


00:06:11.668 --> 00:06:13.512
and he got down on one knee
and everything.


00:06:13.668 --> 00:06:17.072
- He proposed on his birthday?
- I don't understand.


00:06:17.228 --> 00:06:18.995
I'm in love with him.


00:06:19.988 --> 00:06:21.996
That's really great,
sweetie, but...


00:06:22.147 --> 00:06:24.188
You're only 24 years old.


00:06:24.347 --> 00:06:26.191
Nobody gets married
at 24 anymore.


00:06:26.347 --> 00:06:28.191
People get married
when they're 17.


00:06:28.347 --> 00:06:29.711
Not white girls
from New Jersey.


00:06:29.867 --> 00:06:31.427
- Shh!
- Would you listen to yourself?


00:06:31.587 --> 00:06:33.191
No, you listen -
you have made some


00:06:33.346 --> 00:06:35.550
very questionable decisions
in your life.


00:06:35.706 --> 00:06:37.070
Please don't
add to the list


00:06:37.226 --> 00:06:40.915
by marrying some loser kid
with zero future.


00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:44.034
OK. I have an idea.


00:06:44.186 --> 00:06:48.234
If you think he's such a loser,
then don't come to the wedding!


00:06:52.665 --> 00:06:54.345
Jesus, turn that thing down!


00:06:56.705 --> 00:07:01.146
Down volume!
Down volume!


00:07:01.305 --> 00:07:04.545
- Oh, God!
- Down volume!


00:07:10.465 --> 00:07:13.705
You guys, it's getting late.
The party's over, OK?


00:07:13.864 --> 00:07:15.632
Love you. 'Bye.


00:07:15.784 --> 00:07:17.268
Amy, did you see Ethan?


00:07:18.424 --> 00:07:19.865
Baby?


00:07:20.024 --> 00:07:22.184
Ethan?


00:07:26.143 --> 00:07:27.551
Ethan?


00:07:27.703 --> 00:07:30.027
Uh, it's...
Gimme a sec.


00:07:30.183 --> 00:07:32.551
Come on. I want to
get everybody out of here.


00:07:46.822 --> 00:07:48.862
Hey, how's it going with
the, uh, couples counsellor?


00:07:49.022 --> 00:07:51.586
I don't know.
She's so non-specific.


00:07:51.742 --> 00:07:54.382
It's like talking to fog.


00:07:54.542 --> 00:07:56.702
David and I know
where we stand with each other.


00:07:56.861 --> 00:07:59.229
That's how we've lasted this long.
Somehow, it works.


00:07:59.382 --> 00:08:02.906
Well, don't look at me.
I just pretend Terry's invisible.


00:08:03.061 --> 00:08:05.581
- Notice anything different?
- I sure do.


00:08:05.741 --> 00:08:07.465
Nice new mini fridge.


00:08:07.621 --> 00:08:09.062
I think it really
ties the room together.


00:08:09.221 --> 00:08:11.665
-It's the Max 5950.
-It's the one you recommended.


00:08:11.821 --> 00:08:13.708
From the patio series.
Good move.


00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.901
Let's take a look
in the mini ice compartment.


00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.100
Oh, boy.
It's really big, isn't it?


00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:22.348
Now, this stuff is huge
in Europe.


00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.987
And we've just landed
the American campaign.


00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:26.700
- No kidding? Congrats.
- Thanks.


00:08:26.859 --> 00:08:28.867
Russians like it
for breakfast.


00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.267
Before the devil
knows you're dead.


00:08:36.619 --> 00:08:38.386
Boy, it's, um...


00:08:38.539 --> 00:08:40.066
Well...
Really not very good, is it?


00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:42.063
-It's not good at all. No.
- No.


00:08:47.659 --> 00:08:49.142
What's up
with these sheets?


00:08:50.458 --> 00:08:52.499
You, um...


00:08:52.658 --> 00:08:54.458
...spending a little extra time
out here?


00:08:54.618 --> 00:08:56.779
Just a couple of nights a week.


00:08:56.938 --> 00:08:59.306
Late-night TV.


00:09:23.217 --> 00:09:26.021
You've gotta be
fucking kidding me.


00:09:33.016 --> 00:09:35.056
Oh, sh...


00:09:47.375 --> 00:09:48.902
Nina? Wow!


00:09:49.055 --> 00:09:51.859
- David. Hi.
- It's been so long.


00:09:53.294 --> 00:09:56.055
I thought you weren't
coming back for Thanksgiving.


00:09:56.215 --> 00:09:58.102
Yeah, well...


00:09:58.254 --> 00:10:00.022
Um...


00:10:01.574 --> 00:10:04.739
Are my parents here?
Locked out.


00:10:04.894 --> 00:10:07.142
They're in the back.


00:10:07.294 --> 00:10:09.934
Last day of barbecue season.


00:10:12.373 --> 00:10:14.654
What's going on?


00:10:14.813 --> 00:10:16.417
- You OK?
- David?


00:10:16.573 --> 00:10:18.973
Paige wants to know what
you did with the tong thing.


00:10:20.373 --> 00:10:22.053
Hi, Mom.


00:10:22.213 --> 00:10:25.333
I'm back for Thanksgiving.


00:10:25.492 --> 00:10:27.653
We turned it into
a second den.


00:10:27.812 --> 00:10:29.460
If your father's
in the first den


00:10:29.612 --> 00:10:31.172
and I want some privacy,
I come here.


00:10:31.333 --> 00:10:32.696
Honey,
I have this really cool


00:10:32.853 --> 00:10:34.173
self-inflating mattress.


00:10:34.332 --> 00:10:36.897
It fits perfectly in the corner
and it is really comfy.


00:10:39.292 --> 00:10:41.780
But, you know, we have your
old bed frame out there in the...


00:10:41.932 --> 00:10:43.819
...in the garage -
I can set it up for you.


00:10:43.972 --> 00:10:46.100
- Take me two...two se...
- No, that's fine.


00:10:46.251 --> 00:10:48.171
I'll only be here
a few days.


00:10:48.331 --> 00:10:50.776
Why? Where are you
going to now?


00:10:50.931 --> 00:10:53.376
I don't know.


00:10:55.131 --> 00:10:57.051
I haven't figured it out yet.


00:10:57.211 --> 00:10:59.098
Well, why don't you
stay here for a while?


00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:00.691
I don't care -
it's not like we haven't


00:11:00.851 --> 00:11:03.012
gotten used
to you being gone.


00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:05.610
Can you hold off
on the guilt trips


00:11:05.771 --> 00:11:07.091
for just a little while,
please?


00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.811
I've had
a rough couple days.


00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.330
I'd never seen Nina
with her tail between her legs.


00:11:13.489 --> 00:11:16.130
But I didn't
have time to gloat.


00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:19.334
Back on our side of the street,
we had our own problems.


00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:20.854
That's not what I'm saying.


00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:22.974
- What about Christmas?
- Come on, Paige.


00:11:23.129 --> 00:11:26.250
- I'm trying here.
- Oh. Now I'm not trying.


00:11:27.489 --> 00:11:29.136
Can't we have
a simple conversation?


00:11:29.289 --> 00:11:33.173
- I make one suggestion...
- I don't want to go down there.


00:11:33.329 --> 00:11:36.090
- You seem oblivious...
- Come on, Paige...


00:11:43.088 --> 00:11:45.336
I apologise
for what I said about Ethan.


00:11:45.488 --> 00:11:48.249
- Were you waiting for me?
- I'm not your enemy. Nina!


00:11:48.408 --> 00:11:49.892
When you're a parent
some day,


00:11:50.048 --> 00:11:51.456
you'll understand
what it feels like


00:11:51.607 --> 00:11:53.407
to have your child hate you.


00:11:54.448 --> 00:11:56.335
In case you're wondering,
that's your cue to say,


00:11:56.487 --> 00:11:57.808
"I don't hate you, Mom."


00:11:57.967 --> 00:11:59.375
I don't hate you.


00:11:59.527 --> 00:12:04.252
I just get furious
thinking someone has hurt you.


00:12:07.887 --> 00:12:11.291
Don't think I'm crazy.
This is just a thought. But, uh...


00:12:12.687 --> 00:12:15.054
Toby's coming home
for Thanksgiving.


00:12:16.806 --> 00:12:19.327
- Oh, my God.
- He's gotten very attractive.


00:12:19.486 --> 00:12:20.849
That's all I'm saying.


00:12:21.006 --> 00:12:22.926
He works for
the Federal Trade Commission.


00:12:23.086 --> 00:12:24.449
Terrific. You date him.


00:12:24.606 --> 00:12:26.406
Well, it's not like you two
don't have history.


00:12:26.566 --> 00:12:28.094
- We kissed!
- Yeah.


00:12:28.245 --> 00:12:29.566
Once, like, 10 years ago.


00:12:29.725 --> 00:12:32.169
Can you at least let me unpack
before pimping me out?


00:12:32.326 --> 00:12:35.010
OK, fine. But I'm gonna
tell you this for your own good.


00:12:35.165 --> 00:12:37.969
You need to have a real
relationship with a real man.


00:12:38.125 --> 00:12:40.569
It's time you grew up already!
Stop running away.


00:12:40.724 --> 00:12:43.725
You know, you're right.
I'm being selfish.


00:12:43.884 --> 00:12:45.325
The best thing
I can do right now


00:12:45.485 --> 00:12:46.805
is fulfil
your insane suburban fantasy


00:12:46.964 --> 00:12:48.285
where I marry
your best friend's son.


00:12:48.444 --> 00:12:51.849
Now, you go call the catering hall
and I'll lube my vagina.


00:12:52.004 --> 00:12:54.448
That was uncalled for.


00:12:54.604 --> 00:12:56.087
Uh, there's 12 of us
in the delegation.


00:12:56.244 --> 00:12:57.804
I'm really just...
just assisting my boss.


00:12:57.964 --> 00:12:59.928
But the goal is to
tie our trade agreements


00:13:00.083 --> 00:13:01.851
to stricter
environmental regulations


00:13:02.003 --> 00:13:04.131
since things
are kind of a mess over there.


00:13:05.523 --> 00:13:08.087
- China. That's great.
- Yeah, thanks.


00:13:08.243 --> 00:13:10.043
You are gonna have
a great experience.


00:13:10.203 --> 00:13:12.526
- Yeah. Yeah.
- It's, like, a 30-hour flight.


00:13:12.683 --> 00:13:14.723
- Honey, what about Christmas?
- Don't worry, Mom.


00:13:14.882 --> 00:13:16.203
I fly back on the 24th.


00:13:16.362 --> 00:13:17.890
That sounds
really great, Toby.


00:13:18.042 --> 00:13:20.803
I hear that ultimate frisbee
is exploding over there.


00:13:20.962 --> 00:13:23.046
In China. The, uh...


00:13:23.203 --> 00:13:26.684
The Beijing club team
came in second at the World's.


00:13:26.842 --> 00:13:28.446
If I see a game,
I'll let 'em know


00:13:28.602 --> 00:13:31.645
I grew up across the street
from the guy who invented it.


00:13:31.802 --> 00:13:35.370
Well. It wasn't just me. It was
also Jared Kass and, uh...


00:13:35.522 --> 00:13:37.169
- Honey?
- Joel Silver.


00:13:37.322 --> 00:13:38.926
Of course, Joel gets
most of the, you know...


00:13:39.081 --> 00:13:41.766
...most of the play, being
a big movie producer and all.


00:13:41.921 --> 00:13:44.169
Finally!


00:13:46.601 --> 00:13:48.729
Where there's dessert,
there's hope.


00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:56.121
Your mom told me about what
happened with that Ethan guy.


00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:58.200
You OK?


00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:03.000
Yeah.


00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:05.288
I'm good, thanks.


00:14:06.599 --> 00:14:08.519
So, what about you?


00:14:08.679 --> 00:14:10.688
How's the liquor
advertising business going?


00:14:10.839 --> 00:14:12.607
Still pushing booze
onto minors?


00:14:12.759 --> 00:14:15.203
Yes, I am.


00:14:15.359 --> 00:14:16.679
Actually,
I just got a promotion.


00:14:16.839 --> 00:14:18.366
I'm now executive
vice-president,


00:14:18.519 --> 00:14:19.839
creative accounts.


00:14:19.998 --> 00:14:21.526
Congratulations.


00:14:21.679 --> 00:14:23.807
Was that something
you wanted?


00:14:23.958 --> 00:14:25.999
Not really.


00:14:26.158 --> 00:14:28.078
You want me to spoon this
onto the plates?


00:14:28.238 --> 00:14:29.722
Please.


00:14:29.878 --> 00:14:33.359
Uh... Don't just eat it
right out the carton.


00:14:36.078 --> 00:14:38.958
Is it good?


00:14:41.157 --> 00:14:42.565
- It's cold.
- What?


00:14:42.718 --> 00:14:46.722
Hey. I brought that ice-cream
for the pies.


00:14:46.877 --> 00:14:48.764
He made me eat it.


00:14:49.997 --> 00:14:51.765
Well, Cathy wants
to serve dessert.


00:14:51.917 --> 00:14:53.685
Will you please
bring in some plates?


00:14:55.956 --> 00:14:58.324
I still need Christmas lists
from everyone by tonight.


00:14:58.477 --> 00:14:59.797
I'm leaving early tomorrow.


00:14:59.956 --> 00:15:01.964
- Black Friday.
- Don't make fun.


00:15:02.116 --> 00:15:05.924
Last year, I got there at 3am
and I was still 210 in line.


00:15:06.076 --> 00:15:07.516
Why would anyone
want to shop


00:15:07.676 --> 00:15:09.281
on the same day
as everyone else?


00:15:09.436 --> 00:15:11.356
I hear that
they have fist fights


00:15:11.516 --> 00:15:13.240
and people throw their children
at each other.


00:15:13.396 --> 00:15:16.244
Terry! No.
It's really a very...


00:15:16.395 --> 00:15:20.279
Very communal, Christmassy
experience. It's beautiful.


00:15:20.435 --> 00:15:21.799
Listen, I know it's late,


00:15:21.955 --> 00:15:23.439
but I think
we should have a toast.


00:15:23.595 --> 00:15:25.963
It's Thanksgiving. We have
so much to be thankful for.


00:15:26.115 --> 00:15:28.275
Toby is going to China.


00:15:28.434 --> 00:15:29.755
Very exciting.


00:15:29.915 --> 00:15:32.479
Nina is finally
back at home.


00:15:32.635 --> 00:15:35.396
And Vanessa
continues to live among us,


00:15:35.554 --> 00:15:37.234
bringing us joy every day.


00:15:37.394 --> 00:15:39.281
To the Walling
and Ostroff clans.


00:15:39.434 --> 00:15:43.002
Who knew that two families
could get this close?


00:15:43.154 --> 00:15:44.474
Hear, hear.


00:15:44.633 --> 00:15:47.198
I still think we could be
a little closer.


00:15:49.193 --> 00:15:51.474
Well said.


00:15:53.513 --> 00:15:56.601
Man, I thought your mom
was going to applaud


00:15:56.753 --> 00:15:58.074
when she saw us
leave together.


00:15:58.233 --> 00:16:01.081
The woman
is a total lunatic.


00:16:01.233 --> 00:16:03.077
In the first three years
I was gone,


00:16:03.233 --> 00:16:05.033
she sent me
letters from the cat.


00:16:05.192 --> 00:16:07.440
"Dear Nina,
Don't be difficult.


00:16:07.593 --> 00:16:09.000
"Call your mother
on her birthday."


00:16:09.152 --> 00:16:11.520
That's great, actually.
I kind of like that.


00:16:11.672 --> 00:16:14.160
Now you understand
why I never came back.


00:16:15.192 --> 00:16:17.275
Yeah. No, I hear ya. But...


00:16:17.432 --> 00:16:19.952
I'm glad you did.


00:16:21.271 --> 00:16:22.319
Shut up.


00:16:26.471 --> 00:16:28.195
Dance with me.


00:16:29.831 --> 00:16:31.315
Totally.


00:16:34.991 --> 00:16:36.551
You OK?


00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:38.031
I need to get some water.


00:16:38.191 --> 00:16:40.078
- Can I get some water?
- OK. Sit down, wild man.


00:16:40.231 --> 00:16:43.712
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.


00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.554
- Hey.
- Toby needs water.


00:16:50.709 --> 00:16:52.477
What are you doing up?


00:16:52.629 --> 00:16:55.837
Just watching a little TV
in the man cave.


00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:59.110
- Man cave?
- It's the pool house.


00:16:59.269 --> 00:17:02.030
I got one of those
worldwide sports...


00:17:02.189 --> 00:17:04.317
...something something package
your dad recommended.


00:17:04.469 --> 00:17:06.673
There's this
Korean basketball league


00:17:06.829 --> 00:17:08.476
which is completely crazy.


00:17:08.629 --> 00:17:10.757
You know, it's not good
to eat peanut butter


00:17:10.908 --> 00:17:12.229
this late at night.


00:17:12.388 --> 00:17:13.709
It'll make you fat.


00:17:13.868 --> 00:17:15.712
I'm not fat.


00:17:15.868 --> 00:17:17.593
You will be if you
keep eating like that


00:17:17.748 --> 00:17:19.068
at 2:00 in the morning.


00:17:19.228 --> 00:17:20.875
And where'd you pick
this little factoid up?


00:17:21.028 --> 00:17:22.632
I worked in
a lot of restaurants.


00:17:22.787 --> 00:17:24.915
Restaurants
that serve peanut butter?


00:17:25.068 --> 00:17:27.076
Look, do whatever you want.


00:17:27.228 --> 00:17:29.672
I'm just saying
that you wouldn't look good fat.


00:17:32.147 --> 00:17:34.034
I should get back downstairs.


00:17:34.187 --> 00:17:35.954
Yeah, make your mother
very happy. You know that.


00:17:36.107 --> 00:17:37.427
It's what I live for.


00:18:24.824 --> 00:18:26.744
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:18:27.944 --> 00:18:29.471
What happened to Toby?


00:18:29.624 --> 00:18:31.544
I cut him up
in little pieces


00:18:31.704 --> 00:18:33.504
and put him in the fridge
for later.


00:18:40.703 --> 00:18:42.263
Who's playing?


00:18:43.863 --> 00:18:45.707
I have no idea.


00:18:45.863 --> 00:18:47.707
It's...it's the, um...


00:18:50.063 --> 00:18:52.146
...guys in red against the...
the guys in white.


00:18:52.303 --> 00:18:53.950
- White. I got it.
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:18:54.103 --> 00:18:56.111
Go, reds.


00:18:56.262 --> 00:18:57.943
Or White.


00:18:58.102 --> 00:18:59.782
You know.


00:19:43.499 --> 00:19:45.507
Oh, fuck.


00:19:48.499 --> 00:19:51.827
One bedroom, high ceilings.
Close to the PATH train.


00:19:51.979 --> 00:19:53.779
Ooh, washer dryer.


00:19:53.939 --> 00:19:56.503
- Plus it's crazy bright.
- Yeah.


00:19:56.658 --> 00:19:59.223
Well, that's morning light.


00:19:59.379 --> 00:20:01.223
I don't want that.


00:20:01.378 --> 00:20:04.227
Wow, that's, like,
your best excuse in two weeks.


00:20:04.378 --> 00:20:05.938
Hello, Koosers.


00:20:06.099 --> 00:20:08.018
- Did you sell that dresser?
- I did not.


00:20:08.178 --> 00:20:09.618
She's not interested
in the apartment, Henry.


00:20:09.778 --> 00:20:11.099
I told you.


00:20:11.258 --> 00:20:12.786
What?


00:20:12.938 --> 00:20:14.542
What do you mean,
"I told you"?


00:20:14.698 --> 00:20:17.382
You've been talking about
moving out for two years.


00:20:17.537 --> 00:20:19.305
You know what?
I'm saving money. Alright?


00:20:19.457 --> 00:20:21.465
I have a very definite plan.


00:20:21.617 --> 00:20:23.821
You mean that "stay at home,
corrode your soul" plan?


00:20:23.977 --> 00:20:25.941
No, no - the plan
where I move to the city


00:20:26.097 --> 00:20:27.581
and I work with
a big designer.


00:20:27.737 --> 00:20:29.865
I've already made
serious contacts.


00:20:30.017 --> 00:20:31.861
From where'?


00:20:32.017 --> 00:20:37.298
Huffman Koos? Well, you know me
and her and Marlon.


00:20:37.456 --> 00:20:40.141
Hey, I'm serious.
We're worried about you.


00:20:40.296 --> 00:20:42.456
OK, thank you.
I got it under control.


00:20:42.616 --> 00:20:44.143
You guys
go worry about yourselves.


00:20:47.096 --> 00:20:48.896
Wow. There she is'


00:20:49.055 --> 00:20:52.263
1 pm. Very impressive.


00:20:52.416 --> 00:20:54.696
So? Did you have fun
last night?


00:20:54.855 --> 00:20:56.535
I'm sure you'd love
a full report.


00:20:56.695 --> 00:20:58.704
You know,
some mothers and daughters


00:20:58.855 --> 00:21:01.495
actually talk about
these things, like friends.


00:21:01.654 --> 00:21:03.782
It's not happening.


00:21:03.935 --> 00:21:07.743
Well, maybe Toby will be
better company than you.


00:21:07.894 --> 00:21:09.302
Hi!


00:21:15.694 --> 00:21:17.418
Try and control yourself.


00:21:22.093 --> 00:21:23.337
Hey, Nina.


00:21:23.493 --> 00:21:26.537
- Morning, Cathy.
- Good morning, Tobias.


00:21:26.693 --> 00:21:29.334
- Uh, you forgot your sweater.
- Thank you.


00:21:29.493 --> 00:21:31.293
Can I get you
some breakfast, honey?


00:21:31.453 --> 00:21:33.657
No, thanks. I'm OK. Thanks.


00:21:35.132 --> 00:21:37.141
Well, I'll give you two
some privacy.


00:21:37.293 --> 00:21:40.020
There you are.


00:21:43.333 --> 00:21:45.133
I can hear you
hovering out there!


00:21:45.292 --> 00:21:46.820
Fine.


00:21:48.132 --> 00:21:49.813
You're looking a little crispy
this morning.


00:21:49.972 --> 00:21:52.013
Oh, thank you.
You can really put 'em away.


00:21:52.172 --> 00:21:54.933
Did I, uh...
Did I pass out?


00:21:55.092 --> 00:21:56.936
Yeah. Mmm, pretty much.


00:21:57.091 --> 00:21:59.295
Sorry about that.


00:21:59.451 --> 00:22:01.972
- No.
- Um...


00:22:03.131 --> 00:22:04.931
Look.
Uh, I was thinking.


00:22:05.091 --> 00:22:09.500
I had a really fun time last night
before passing out, and...


00:22:09.651 --> 00:22:11.779
...I'm supposed to have dinner
with my folks tonight.


00:22:11.931 --> 00:22:14.615
And being as
I'm leaving in two days,


00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:19.331
I thought, you know,
maybe you'd like to join us


00:22:19.490 --> 00:22:21.618
so we could
hang out more.


00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:26.734
Yeah. Dinner with you and
your parents, it...sounds great.


00:22:31.769 --> 00:22:33.973
- Come on, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:35.809 --> 00:22:37.457
Alright. OK.


00:22:37.609 --> 00:22:39.529
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:39.689 --> 00:22:43.378
Toby, it's called
the fast-moving tile game.


00:22:43.529 --> 00:22:45.449
Hold.


00:22:48.289 --> 00:22:50.176
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold!


00:22:50.328 --> 00:22:52.696
OK. OK.


00:22:52.849 --> 00:22:54.496
Actually,
just go out ahead of me.


00:22:54.648 --> 00:22:56.372
Oh!


00:22:56.528 --> 00:22:59.048
5, the 13. I'm out!


00:22:59.208 --> 00:23:01.815
- What?
- Ah. Yes.


00:23:01.968 --> 00:23:03.528
Now, who's gonna help me
with the dishes?


00:23:03.688 --> 00:23:05.171
I will, Mom. Wait.


00:23:05.328 --> 00:23:07.248
Hang on a sec.
I gotta take this. It's work.


00:23:07.407 --> 00:23:08.967
This is Toby.


00:23:09.127 --> 00:23:10.611
Oh, hello, sir.


00:23:10.767 --> 00:23:12.088
Uh-huh.


00:23:12.247 --> 00:23:13.567
- No, no, it's no problem.
- Yeah.


00:23:13.727 --> 00:23:15.407
I think maybe
I'll go pick up a movie


00:23:15.567 --> 00:23:17.050
in case you want to
watch something later.


00:23:17.207 --> 00:23:20.011
- That sounds fun.
- I'll come with you.


00:23:20.166 --> 00:23:22.774
Keep you company
while Toby does the dishes.


00:23:33.366 --> 00:23:34.729
Look.


00:23:34.886 --> 00:23:37.929
What happened last night
was a mistake.


00:23:38.086 --> 00:23:40.334
- OK?
- No, you're right.


00:23:43.085 --> 00:23:46.250
Relax, OK?
It was nothing.


00:23:46.405 --> 00:23:48.609
And you stopped it.
You're absolved.


00:23:58.924 --> 00:24:00.572
Hello in there?


00:24:00.724 --> 00:24:02.285
Is there anyone in there?


00:24:02.444 --> 00:24:05.368
You just have to
instigate trouble.


00:24:05.524 --> 00:24:08.328
I do not instigate trouble.


00:24:08.484 --> 00:24:09.804
Well, OK.


00:24:09.963 --> 00:24:11.491
Well, then, Why'd you
come to dinner tonight?


00:24:11.643 --> 00:24:12.964
Toby invited me.


00:24:13.123 --> 00:24:14.891
And now that we're
talking about instigators,


00:24:15.043 --> 00:24:16.887
you leaned into me.


00:24:17.043 --> 00:24:18.604
I leaned into you?


00:24:18.763 --> 00:24:20.607
- I leaned... I did not lean.
- Yes, you did.


00:24:20.763 --> 00:24:22.324
- You leaned into me.
- What?!


00:24:22.483 --> 00:24:24.491
Oh... He said, she said.


00:24:26.162 --> 00:24:27.483
He said, she said.


00:24:27.642 --> 00:24:29.322
Where did that come from?


00:24:29.482 --> 00:24:31.402
I have no idea
where that came from.


00:24:37.602 --> 00:24:39.446
I'm not instigating.


00:25:04.880 --> 00:25:06.244
I've been thinking
about getting


00:25:06.400 --> 00:25:08.409
one of those
giant electric snow globes.


00:25:08.560 --> 00:25:11.604
You ever seen one of those?
Really big ones?


00:25:11.760 --> 00:25:13.768
Fantastic.


00:25:13.920 --> 00:25:15.884
Mom?


00:25:16.039 --> 00:25:18.123
We're in here, honey.


00:25:18.279 --> 00:25:20.767
I'm going out.


00:25:20.919 --> 00:25:23.003
Well!


00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:25.680
Well, don't you look nice?


00:25:25.839 --> 00:25:27.367
Thanks.


00:25:27.519 --> 00:25:28.960
So is Toby
taking you somewhere?


00:25:29.119 --> 00:25:31.880
- Uh, yeah.
- OK. OK.


00:25:32.039 --> 00:25:33.403
- Fine.
- Mom!


00:25:33.559 --> 00:25:35.283
Give me some room.


00:25:35.438 --> 00:25:37.719
Fine. Have fun.


00:25:41.638 --> 00:25:43.243
Is she eating with us?


00:25:43.398 --> 00:25:46.279
Toby is taking her out.
She was all dressed up.


00:25:46.438 --> 00:25:48.162
- Toby already left for DC.
- What?


00:25:48.318 --> 00:25:49.725
Yeah, first thing
this morning.


00:25:49.878 --> 00:25:51.722
Some congressman wanted
to be with the delegation


00:25:51.877 --> 00:25:53.438
before they went to China.


00:26:22.916 --> 00:26:25.916
"Left this morning."
Oh, shit!


00:26:38.074 --> 00:26:40.158
- H-hello?
- Mom?


00:26:40.315 --> 00:26:42.323
Listen. I lied earlier.


00:26:42.474 --> 00:26:44.242
I'm not going out with Toby.


00:26:44.394 --> 00:26:46.118
He actually left for Washington
this morning.


00:26:46.274 --> 00:26:49.001
- Oh?
- Yeah.


00:26:49.154 --> 00:26:53.321
I'm meeting Meredith Lovett.
Remember her?


00:26:53.474 --> 00:26:55.797
I didn't tell you because
I know you don't like her.


00:26:55.954 --> 00:27:00.002
Oh, honey, thank you.
Thank you for telling me.


00:27:00.153 --> 00:27:03.961
You know...
You don't have to lie to me.


00:27:04.113 --> 00:27:06.154
I know.


00:27:06.313 --> 00:27:08.037
So where are you going?


00:27:09.633 --> 00:27:12.841
Uh, we're going to the Regal
to see a movie.


00:27:14.832 --> 00:27:16.153
Uh, Mom?


00:27:16.312 --> 00:27:18.832
Thanks...for being so cool


00:27:18.992 --> 00:27:21.240
and letting me come back
and stay and everything.


00:27:21.392 --> 00:27:24.240
I've been feeling really
tossed around lately, so...


00:27:24.391 --> 00:27:27.796
You know.
Thanks for being there.


00:27:29.272 --> 00:27:31.672
OK, well...
I'll see you later for dinner.


00:27:36.631 --> 00:27:38.191
Oh, my...


00:28:15.029 --> 00:28:16.273
Whoa!


00:28:16.429 --> 00:28:18.470
Cathy.


00:28:18.629 --> 00:28:20.832
- What are you...?
- I'm, uh...


00:28:20.989 --> 00:28:23.433
- What are you...
- I'm not, uh... Nothing.


00:28:23.589 --> 00:28:27.113
Paige and I had a fight,
and I spent the night here. So...


00:28:29.028 --> 00:28:31.472
Oh, my God!


00:28:31.628 --> 00:28:33.232
Hey, Nina.


00:28:33.387 --> 00:28:34.828
- What are you...
- Oh, my God!


00:28:34.988 --> 00:28:36.428
Cathy! Slow down.


00:28:36.588 --> 00:28:39.795
Slow down? I can read
an ice bucket, David.


00:28:39.948 --> 00:28:41.989
- Cathy.
- Oh, my God!


00:28:42.147 --> 00:28:44.995
I'm gonna throw up!


00:28:50.106 --> 00:28:52.627
- Jesus, David!
- Paige, listen to me.


00:28:52.787 --> 00:28:54.707
Just tell me how long
it's been going on.


00:28:54.867 --> 00:28:57.027
We kissed. That's it.


00:28:57.187 --> 00:28:59.631
Then what the hell were you
doing in a goddamn motel room?


00:28:59.786 --> 00:29:01.434
This...


00:29:03.186 --> 00:29:05.706
I'm sorry.
The whole thing was wrong.


00:29:05.866 --> 00:29:07.187
But let's be honest.


00:29:07.346 --> 00:29:09.430
Things have not been good
between us for a long time.


00:29:09.585 --> 00:29:11.069
Oh, God, don't do that.


00:29:11.225 --> 00:29:13.625
Don't apologise and then
blame me in the same sentence.


00:29:13.786 --> 00:29:15.794
Come on, Paige.
You're not happy either.


00:29:15.945 --> 00:29:18.346
It's not about
being happy, David!


00:29:18.505 --> 00:29:20.425
Well, then, what is it?


00:29:39.984 --> 00:29:41.752
Jesus, say something already.


00:29:41.904 --> 00:29:43.868
I will say something
when I want.


00:29:44.023 --> 00:29:46.424
You don't get to decide
when I say something. I decide!


00:29:46.584 --> 00:29:49.028
- Then decide already!
- I'll decide.


00:29:49.184 --> 00:29:52.468
You have caused
some serious trouble


00:29:52.624 --> 00:29:53.911
in the past, young lady.


00:29:54.063 --> 00:29:55.471
Don't you
roll your eyes at me.


00:29:55.623 --> 00:29:57.587
I'm sorry, it doesn't work
when you try to play


00:29:57.743 --> 00:29:59.467
the stern father - it looks like
you're pretending.


00:29:59.623 --> 00:30:01.707
Your father is not pretending!
We are furious!


00:30:01.862 --> 00:30:03.270
I'm not pretending.


00:30:03.423 --> 00:30:04.983
David and I,
we like each other.


00:30:05.142 --> 00:30:07.390
- Oh, my God.
- We've always been close.


00:30:07.542 --> 00:30:09.583
It's not like we planned this.
It just happened.


00:30:09.742 --> 00:30:11.347
- You like each other?
- Yeah.


00:30:11.502 --> 00:30:12.823
- Oh, my God.
- Oh, my God!


00:30:12.982 --> 00:30:15.502
I know what this is -
