00:45:05.329 --> 00:45:07.609
he went online and found
a pick-up ultimate frisbee game


00:45:07.768 --> 00:45:09.132
in Paramus.


00:45:09.288 --> 00:45:12.332
Hey, guys! You, uh...
you got room for one more?


00:45:12.488 --> 00:45:14.572
No daylight. No daylight.


00:45:14.728 --> 00:45:19.528
So it was really Jared Kass
and I, and Joel Silver...


00:45:19.688 --> 00:45:21.368
Joel Silver,
the movie producer?


00:45:21.528 --> 00:45:22.772
Yeah. Yeah.


00:45:23.848 --> 00:45:25.331
My mother
had been making herself


00:45:25.487 --> 00:45:27.168
mysteriously unavailable.


00:45:28.327 --> 00:45:30.531
But, as all our neighbours
discovered...


00:45:32.127 --> 00:45:35.292
...she hadn't completely lost sight
of the Christmas spirit.


00:45:40.487 --> 00:45:41.895
Terry!


00:45:42.046 --> 00:45:43.726
Everything was changing.


00:45:43.887 --> 00:45:45.207
Terry!


00:45:45.366 --> 00:45:46.971
No-one even recognised
each other anymore.


00:45:49.806 --> 00:45:52.567
- Smoothie?
- Oh, good God.


00:45:55.646 --> 00:45:57.686
Very good.


00:45:57.846 --> 00:45:59.929
Now kiss the chef.


00:46:11.725 --> 00:46:13.733
Maybe they are
really in love.


00:46:13.885 --> 00:46:15.205
You said it doesn't last.


00:46:15.364 --> 00:46:17.645
You said that the grasses only
wanted the cows for their money.


00:46:17.805 --> 00:46:19.365
Usually that is the case,
but not always.


00:46:19.524 --> 00:46:21.532
- Your dad is pretty cute.
- Don't be gross, OK?


00:46:21.684 --> 00:46:23.528
Just because you haven't gotten
laid in, like, three weeks.


00:46:23.684 --> 00:46:25.648
Perhaps your problem is
more with Nina than your father.


00:46:25.804 --> 00:46:27.571
Oh, is that so, Henry?
Why is that?


00:46:27.724 --> 00:46:29.044
Because maybe
you are jealous,


00:46:29.203 --> 00:46:32.444
because she has travelled
many places and has lived,


00:46:32.604 --> 00:46:35.365
because she takes chances.


00:46:35.523 --> 00:46:36.844
No. You know what?


00:46:37.004 --> 00:46:38.531
You, my friend,
have breathed in


00:46:38.683 --> 00:46:40.527
a little too much
of this cheap pine wax, OK?


00:46:40.683 --> 00:46:43.564
'Cause she's a selfish skank.
And he's selfish too.


00:46:43.723 --> 00:46:46.004
Yeah, but if he
really is happier with her


00:46:46.163 --> 00:46:47.527
and you make him stop,


00:46:47.683 --> 00:46:49.243
then you're the one
who's being selfish.


00:46:51.083 --> 00:46:52.763
That is maybe
the most intelligent thing


00:46:52.922 --> 00:46:54.362
you have ever said.


00:47:10.001 --> 00:47:11.769
Hey.


00:47:11.921 --> 00:47:14.769
What is
Barnyard International?


00:47:14.921 --> 00:47:17.922
Well, um... See those presents
you got at babyGap?


00:47:18.081 --> 00:47:20.209
Instead of giving those
to a baby


00:47:20.360 --> 00:47:21.921
who might already
have lots of clothes,


00:47:22.081 --> 00:47:24.001
why not help a baby
who doesn't have any food?


00:47:24.161 --> 00:47:25.481
They're not for a baby.


00:47:25.640 --> 00:47:27.081
They're for my husband's
new girlfriend.


00:47:29.200 --> 00:47:30.684
Here's some pamphlets.


00:47:33.120 --> 00:47:35.564
"One goat
can provide a family


00:47:35.719 --> 00:47:37.847
"with enough milk
for an entire year."


00:47:39.640 --> 00:47:41.768
It's like the Christmas gift
that keeps giving.


00:47:41.919 --> 00:47:43.479
Yeah. It is.


00:47:43.640 --> 00:47:45.560
That's good. Can I use that?


00:47:45.719 --> 00:47:48.163
Sure.


00:47:55.519 --> 00:47:57.766
Oh, yes! Oh! Oh!


00:48:05.478 --> 00:48:08.478
There are gift receipts inside,
if anyone wants to return them.


00:48:12.118 --> 00:48:13.842
I think after Christmas Eve,


00:48:13.997 --> 00:48:16.442
we should demand
that Paige have dinner with us.


00:48:19.397 --> 00:48:21.077
What are you doing?


00:48:21.237 --> 00:48:22.884
Come here.


00:48:25.037 --> 00:48:27.437
- I have toothpaste in my mouth.
- I don't care.


00:48:32.636 --> 00:48:34.360
Come here.


00:48:45.036 --> 00:48:48.080
OK. Thank you
for dropping me off.


00:48:48.236 --> 00:48:50.277
I got you these.


00:48:55.355 --> 00:48:57.155
Chef's clogs.


00:48:57.315 --> 00:48:59.202
You said after working last night,
your feet hurt, so...


00:48:59.354 --> 00:49:01.034
You're so sweet.


00:49:09.674 --> 00:49:11.518
OK. You're gonna
make me late.


00:49:11.674 --> 00:49:13.474
Whoo!


00:49:23.233 --> 00:49:24.553
- That was fast.
- Yeah.


00:49:24.714 --> 00:49:26.874
Um...


00:49:27.033 --> 00:49:28.517
What?


00:49:30.673 --> 00:49:31.993
Nothing.


00:49:32.152 --> 00:49:33.473
What's up?


00:49:33.633 --> 00:49:34.954
Nothing.


00:49:35.113 --> 00:49:36.717
Come on.
Tell me what's wrong.


00:49:38.632 --> 00:49:40.913
- I...
- I love you, Nina.


00:49:42.872 --> 00:49:46.353
You shit. You suck.
I wanted to say it first.


00:49:48.112 --> 00:49:50.873
Well, now I'm not saying it.
You blew it, buddy.


00:49:52.871 --> 00:49:55.075
I'm just kidding.
I love you too.


00:49:59.991 --> 00:50:02.631
You guys were married
for 28 years.


00:50:02.791 --> 00:50:05.039
If anyone should call,
it should be him.


00:50:05.190 --> 00:50:07.231
- Do you have any perfume?
- No.


00:50:07.390 --> 00:50:10.075
What?! Where are you
even going?


00:50:10.231 --> 00:50:12.631
Well, I read about
a late-evening cabaret show


00:50:12.790 --> 00:50:14.274
that begins at 9:30.


00:50:14.430 --> 00:50:16.678
- I'm taking myself out.
- Cabaret?


00:50:16.831 --> 00:50:18.959
Am I the only one
who's dealing with this?


00:50:19.110 --> 00:50:22.711
I mean, don't you
want to come back home?


00:50:24.669 --> 00:50:26.110
I'm not sure.


00:50:26.270 --> 00:50:28.790
I'm having a good time
for once.


00:50:28.949 --> 00:50:32.877
I'd like to see you
do the same.


00:50:36.469 --> 00:50:37.996
Let's go, guys!
Pick up the pace!


00:50:38.149 --> 00:50:39.829
Hey, Mondo!
Where's my rigatoni? Let's go!


00:50:39.989 --> 00:50:41.473
Bring it up, parmigiana.


00:50:41.629 --> 00:50:43.429
Nina! Plate 27!


00:50:43.588 --> 00:50:44.952
Alright, guys-


00:50:45.108 --> 00:50:47.432
On 24, I got a mahi mahi
and a chicken parmigiana.


00:50:47.588 --> 00:50:49.475
Thanks for sending her to me.
She's a good worker.


00:50:49.628 --> 00:50:51.036
- Well, that's great.
- Chef likes her.


00:50:51.188 --> 00:50:54.353
Haven't seen you and Paige
for a while. It's good to see you.


00:50:54.508 --> 00:50:56.953
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


00:51:25.866 --> 00:51:28.790
- Done with your appetiser, sir?
- Sorry?


00:51:28.946 --> 00:51:30.474
Done with
your appetiser, sir?


00:51:30.625 --> 00:51:32.589
Yeah. That... Yeah.
That's great. Thanks.


00:51:37.306 --> 00:51:38.833
Hello.


00:51:40.145 --> 00:51:41.673
Hi, Paige.


00:51:43.665 --> 00:51:46.152
Nice move
on the Christmas card.


00:51:46.305 --> 00:51:47.952
Thank you.


00:51:48.985 --> 00:51:52.106
- Dining alone?
- Uh, yeah. I guess.


00:51:53.424 --> 00:51:55.268
So how are you doing?
Is everything...


00:51:55.425 --> 00:51:57.225
Sit down. Don't have to
make this uncomfortable.


00:51:57.384 --> 00:51:58.867
Just...


00:52:01.504 --> 00:52:03.752
Plus, you know
how I hate pleasantries.


00:52:05.264 --> 00:52:07.348
What about you?


00:52:07.503 --> 00:52:09.511
You look happy.


00:52:10.904 --> 00:52:12.464
Things are OK.
You know, I'm...


00:52:12.623 --> 00:52:15.068
If you're happy,
you can say so.


00:52:15.223 --> 00:52:16.990
You don't need
to spare my feelings.


00:52:17.143 --> 00:52:21.027
Just...be genuine,
David, please.


00:52:21.183 --> 00:52:22.787
Please.


00:52:25.183 --> 00:52:27.343
Yes. I'm happy-


00:52:30.742 --> 00:52:32.302
Thank you.


00:52:32.462 --> 00:52:34.022
Yeah.


00:52:35.422 --> 00:52:37.342
Look, I know
there's nothing I can say...


00:52:37.502 --> 00:52:38.910
Then don't try.


00:52:39.061 --> 00:52:40.861
Paige, stop. Please.


00:52:41.021 --> 00:52:43.269
This is exactly
how we got to this.


00:52:44.662 --> 00:52:49.103
OK, not exactly.
It's partly.


00:52:49.261 --> 00:52:52.109
We stopped talking
to each other.


00:52:54.461 --> 00:52:57.025
I used to love who I was
around you.


00:52:57.180 --> 00:52:59.908
What happened to us?


00:53:01.460 --> 00:53:03.948
We used to have fun.
Remember that?


00:53:05.900 --> 00:53:08.421
We used to laugh.
God, you were so funny.


00:53:08.580 --> 00:53:10.227
I'm still funny.


00:53:10.380 --> 00:53:12.464
I'm... Ask them.


00:53:34.419 --> 00:53:36.186
Shelly just fired me!


00:53:36.339 --> 00:53:37.866
Hey, hey.


00:53:38.018 --> 00:53:41.345
- What happened?
- Oh! This is fucking bullshit!


00:53:41.498 --> 00:53:44.062
- What? Why?
- Because he's not an idiot.


00:53:44.218 --> 00:53:46.978
He saw you and Paige, and he
saw me, and he figured it out.


00:53:47.138 --> 00:53:49.461
He said he didn't want
to be in the middle of it.


00:53:49.618 --> 00:53:51.626
And I was good at that job!


00:53:51.777 --> 00:53:53.741
Why...


00:53:53.898 --> 00:53:56.178
Why were you talking to her?


00:53:56.337 --> 00:53:58.017
She came into the restaurant.


00:53:58.176 --> 00:54:00.937
What do you expect me to do?


00:54:01.097 --> 00:54:03.420
I saw you sitting with her,
and I just thought...


00:54:05.977 --> 00:54:07.297
Thought what?


00:54:07.457 --> 00:54:09.224
I don't know.


00:54:11.696 --> 00:54:13.584
You looked normal together.


00:54:20.815 --> 00:54:23.423
Can we please get out of here?


00:54:31.494 --> 00:54:32.858
# I really can't stay


00:54:33.014 --> 00:54:34.814
# But, baby,
it's cold outside


00:54:34.975 --> 00:54:37.855
- # I've got to go away
- # But, baby, it's cold outside


00:54:38.015 --> 00:54:39.619
# This evening has been...


00:54:39.774 --> 00:54:41.302
# Been hoping
that you drop in


00:54:41.454 --> 00:54:42.818
# So very nice


00:54:42.974 --> 00:54:46.018
# I'll hold your hands
They're just like ice


00:54:46.174 --> 00:54:47.974
# My mother
will start to worry... I


00:54:48.134 --> 00:54:49.901
Hi. Mrs Ostroff'?


00:54:50.054 --> 00:54:51.701
We've never met.


00:54:51.854 --> 00:54:53.982
But I'm Ethan.


00:54:58.774 --> 00:55:00.498
You're our leader.
You can't quit!


00:55:00.653 --> 00:55:03.894
Christmas Eve is in, like,
six days. They're counting on us.


00:55:04.053 --> 00:55:08.221
Try and calm down. Calm down.


00:55:08.373 --> 00:55:11.254
Calm down. Order!


00:55:11.412 --> 00:55:13.299
I know you're upset.


00:55:13.453 --> 00:55:17.021
But you're all
dedicated and talented singers.


00:55:18.492 --> 00:55:19.813
Marcus will take over
as leader.


00:55:19.972 --> 00:55:22.296
- What?!
- Marcus?


00:55:22.452 --> 00:55:24.416
- Why are you even doing this?
- Yeah.


00:55:24.571 --> 00:55:28.215
Well, I believe these pamphlets
should explain everything.


00:55:28.372 --> 00:55:31.056
Each cow or goat
will allow its recipient


00:55:31.211 --> 00:55:33.819
independence
and self-sufficiency


00:55:33.971 --> 00:55:36.252
for years to come.


00:55:37.251 --> 00:55:39.455
And that's pretty great,
isn't it?


00:55:40.771 --> 00:55:43.619
Shelly, this has
nothing to do with you.


00:55:43.770 --> 00:55:45.614
No, I know it's complicated.


00:55:45.771 --> 00:55:47.855
No. I understand.


00:55:49.290 --> 00:55:51.058
Thanks for calling back.


00:55:53.890 --> 00:55:55.211
Told you.


00:55:55.370 --> 00:55:57.094
He'll write you
a reference, but...


00:55:57.250 --> 00:55:58.854
Yeah. He doesn't
want to get involved.


00:55:59.009 --> 00:56:02.491
This isn't gonna work.
I need to find another job.


00:56:02.650 --> 00:56:04.330
I can't stay at Meredith's
rent-free.


00:56:04.489 --> 00:56:05.810
I know.


00:56:05.970 --> 00:56:07.290
And I can't stay here,


00:56:07.449 --> 00:56:08.857
across the street
from my parents.


00:56:09.009 --> 00:56:11.770
- I love you. But...
- What the fuck?


00:56:11.929 --> 00:56:15.333
- Ethan?
- What the hell is going on?


00:56:15.489 --> 00:56:18.577
- What are you doing here?
- Ethan? Like, Ethan Ethan?


00:56:18.729 --> 00:56:21.610
- How did you get in here?
- Your mom gave me the keys.


00:56:21.768 --> 00:56:23.416
She told me
to let myself in,


00:56:23.568 --> 00:56:25.096
like you might not
hear the bell.


00:56:25.248 --> 00:56:27.768
Look, Ethan, I'm sorry, but I'm
gonna have to ask you to leave.


00:56:27.928 --> 00:56:31.332
You can ask, but I'm not gonna.
Who is this?


00:56:31.487 --> 00:56:33.375
Ethan, this is David -
David and Paige,


00:56:33.528 --> 00:56:35.492
my parents' best friends
from across the street.


00:56:36.727 --> 00:56:38.287
Why are you telling
your parents' friend


00:56:38.448 --> 00:56:39.768
that you love him?


00:56:39.927 --> 00:56:42.175
The door's open.
What's going on?


00:56:42.327 --> 00:56:44.575
Nina, I need to talk to you.


00:56:44.727 --> 00:56:46.811
Can we go somewhere
for, like, five minutes?


00:56:46.967 --> 00:56:48.647
Ethan!
I think you should leave.


00:56:48.807 --> 00:56:51.655
- Ethan Ethan?
- Yes! Just five minutes!


00:56:51.806 --> 00:56:53.726
She said no, Ethan.


00:56:53.886 --> 00:56:56.134
I'm gonna ask you one more time
to get out of here.


00:56:56.287 --> 00:57:00.935
And if I don't, Pops,
what are you gonna do about it?


00:57:01.086 --> 00:57:02.046
Arggh!


00:57:02.205 --> 00:57:03.613
'Dad!
Hey!


00:57:03.766 --> 00:57:04.606
- David!
- Dad!


00:57:04.766 --> 00:57:06.370
Get off me!


00:57:07.806 --> 00:57:10.054
# Your eyes
are like starlight now


00:57:10.205 --> 00:57:11.733
# To break this spell


00:57:11.885 --> 00:57:14.766
# I'll take your hat
Your hair looks swell... #


00:57:14.925 --> 00:57:16.725
Why don't you go fuck...


00:57:16.885 --> 00:57:19.612
- What?
- Nothing.


00:57:19.764 --> 00:57:21.369
Its OK.


00:57:24.044 --> 00:57:28.245
# Baby,
it's cold outside. #


00:57:38.164 --> 00:57:42.092
Yes, I cheated on you.
And for that, I am deeply sorry.


00:57:42.244 --> 00:57:45.332
But here's the thing.
I'm a sabotager.


00:57:45.483 --> 00:57:49.084
See, any time
anything good happens to me,


00:57:49.243 --> 00:57:51.087
I...I...I just try
and ruin it, you know,


00:57:51.243 --> 00:57:52.803
because I get scared.


00:57:52.963 --> 00:57:56.651
Now, things with us
were really...real.


00:57:56.802 --> 00:57:59.410
But I didn't feel like
I deserved you,


00:57:59.562 --> 00:58:03.163
so I became the sabotager
and, like, destroyed it.


00:58:03.322 --> 00:58:05.286
That's great, Ethan.


00:58:05.442 --> 00:58:07.526
But we can't just go on
and pretend like everything's fine


00:58:07.682 --> 00:58:09.210
because you learned
a new term about yourself.


00:58:09.362 --> 00:58:12.931
And I don't even think
'sabotager' is a word.


00:58:13.082 --> 00:58:14.969
OK. Please allow me
to finish.


00:58:15.122 --> 00:58:18.166
See, I think
you're a sabotager also.


00:58:18.321 --> 00:58:21.365
You totally pushed for us
to get married so you could, like,


00:58:21.521 --> 00:58:23.725
prove to your parents
that, you know,


00:58:23.881 --> 00:58:25.289
you were
this responsible person.


00:58:25.441 --> 00:58:29.282
But simultaneously, you were
just trying to piss them off


00:58:29.440 --> 00:58:31.360
by marrying someone like me.


00:58:31.520 --> 00:58:33.048
I've moved on.


00:58:33.201 --> 00:58:35.524
- OK? David and I...
- David and you...


00:58:35.681 --> 00:58:40.045
He's your parents' best friend.
For Christ's sakes.


00:58:40.200 --> 00:58:43.321
I mean, what... Are you gonna move
here to New Jersey?


00:58:43.480 --> 00:58:45.728
You hate it here.


00:58:47.839 --> 00:58:49.160
We're done.


00:58:49.319 --> 00:58:51.447
OK? Go home.


00:58:51.600 --> 00:58:53.127
I only bought
a one-way ticket.


00:58:56.160 --> 00:58:58.168
Well, I'm not giving up
on us, Nina!


00:58:58.319 --> 00:59:00.600
I love you too much
for that!


00:59:03.359 --> 00:59:05.519
What?


00:59:31.997 --> 00:59:33.557
What are you doing
with my bag?


00:59:33.717 --> 00:59:35.725
Huh? Nothing.
Just getting it some air.


00:59:37.957 --> 00:59:40.118
- Give me my bag.
- No.


00:59:40.277 --> 00:59:42.480
Give me my bag!


00:59:42.637 --> 00:59:45.801
- Eat me, dick slut.
- Give me my bag, Vanessa!


00:59:45.956 --> 00:59:47.439
No, Nina!


00:59:47.596 --> 00:59:49.516
- No!
- Give me my bag!


00:59:49.676 --> 00:59:53.036
- No! No!
- Give it to me!


00:59:53.196 --> 00:59:54.517
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Give it!


00:59:54.676 --> 00:59:56.159
Oh!


01:00:31.233 --> 01:00:33.077
Oh, honey. Uh...


01:00:33.234 --> 01:00:34.914
Honey?


01:00:35.073 --> 01:00:36.993
I'm sorry, Dad.


01:00:37.153 --> 01:00:38.953
Uh...


01:00:44.512 --> 01:00:46.673
Oh...


01:00:59.672 --> 01:01:02.476
Uh, you know, leave it be.
It's a...it's a badge of honour.


01:01:02.631 --> 01:01:04.072
- You sure?
- Yeah.


01:01:04.232 --> 01:01:06.076
There's aloe on the pad
to prevent scarring.


01:01:06.231 --> 01:01:07.715
OK. Um...


01:01:07.871 --> 01:01:13.240
You know, I'm good.
I'm, uh...I'm good.


01:01:15.230 --> 01:01:17.598
I'm so sorry about
all this horrible...


01:01:18.991 --> 01:01:20.518
...stuff.


01:01:21.791 --> 01:01:23.319
I'm just...


01:01:24.671 --> 01:01:26.515
Yeah.


01:01:29.790 --> 01:01:33.478
You know,
my parents were kinda weird.


01:01:33.630 --> 01:01:36.434
That's why I'm, um...


01:01:37.790 --> 01:01:42.394
Sometimes it's really hard
to say everything you want to.


01:01:42.549 --> 01:01:44.109
You know...


01:01:45.589 --> 01:01:49.997
Your father, he loves you.


01:01:51.189 --> 01:01:54.189
Just don't let that
get confused


01:01:54.348 --> 01:01:56.596
with everything
that's happening.


01:02:00.748 --> 01:02:02.111
Life.


01:02:02.268 --> 01:02:03.588
Ooph!


